<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="045d" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Invoice-family rows re-derive their five resolver fields on a generic create and on an update that sets or changes their core lookup (Q8 (a))</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService (follow-up to 045, 045b, 045c)</phase>
    <gate>045a, 045b and 045c merged into the work branch (c1afee6e02 or later). Owner go 2026-11-12. UAC-r2 reviews the diff before merge.</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes what the generic create and the generic update paths write on six tables (.cs, bff-api); changes the pre-write rule contract; access-rule adjacent; modifies tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fail-closed reasoning on the create's step order and on two update path families with different readers.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits RecordTableRules, RecordCreationService and OwnedChildWrite, which 045b and 045c just changed.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>045a, 045b, 045c</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, field-mapping, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 session</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Rule (owner ruling Q8 (a), 2026-11-07; owner go 2026-11-12): an invoice-family row (sprk_invoice, sprk_billingevent, sprk_invoicesubmission, sprk_invoiceapproval, sprk_externalidentifier, sprk_invoicecorrection) written through a generic path carries the five resolver fields (record type, id, name, url, number) of the core record it names, derived by the server from that record. On a create the fields are derived whenever the row is admitted. On an update they are derived when the update sets or clears one of the row's own core lookups. The derive is the one the dedicated writers already use (`InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard.DeriveResolverFieldsAsync`). Design: `notes/task-045c-notes.md`, section "Q8 (a): invoice-family re-derivation on a generic write. Deferred to 045d".</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, BFF write path. Security fails closed. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>No generic create of a family row, and no generic caller update that moves a family row's core lookup, writes the row without the five fields describing the core record it names. A failed derive writes nothing.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
Shape (045c notes, "Proposed shape"):
1. The pre-write delegate returns a result: `PreWriteCheck: Task&lt;PreWriteResult&gt;`, where `PreWriteResult` is a `PreWriteRefusal` or additional columns. The refusal factories (`Refused`, `Failed`, `NotFound`, `Undecided`) are unchanged.
2. `RecordTableRules.InvoiceFamilyRule` builds the columns from the decision the guard already makes (`InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard.Check`), then `DeriveResolverFieldsAsync` and `InvoiceFamilyResolverFields.ToFields()` (all five whole, or none).
3. Create step 5½ (`RecordCreationService.RunPreWriteRulesAsync`) returns the merged columns; step 5½ applies them to `item` before step 6. Columns the caller set are overwritten: the pair must describe the core lookup the row names.
4. Update: when the body sets or changes the row's own core lookup, the same derive runs and the five columns join the PATCH body. The reader is the one the path already has.

Order (045c notes, "Evidence"): on the create, the derive reads the regarded record app-only, as the dedicated writers do, so it runs only AFTER step 5's caller AppendTo on every record the row names. On the caller update paths the derive reads as the caller, so Dataverse decides what the caller may read. On the app-only update paths (playbook Update Record, output mapping, field-mapping push) the derive reads app-only through the `IGenericEntityService` the path already holds, after that path's invoice-family guard and planner.

Decision (owner, 2026-11-12, option (b)): on the generic paths the row takes what the record has. The type, the id and the URL are always written; the name and the number are written when the record has them, and cleared otherwise. A blank name or number on a generic path is not a refusal. The dedicated submission writers keep their all-five-or-refuse derive unchanged.

Decision (main session, 2026-11-12; the proposal's open point 2): a derive failure (`ReadFailedCode`, `ResolverFieldsIncompleteCode`, `RecordNotFoundCode`) maps through the EXISTING invoice-family refusal mapping: `RecordTableRules.InvoiceFamilyPreWrite` on the create, the route's existing invoice-family mapping on an update (`ChildRecordEndpoints.InvoiceFamilyRefused`, the chat tool's `RefileRefusal`). The write is refused (fail closed). A row whose core lookup changed is never written without its five fields. The refusal contract (NFR-07) is unchanged byte for byte: the same codes, statuses and texts.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs (PreWriteCheck, PreWriteRow, PreWriteRule, InvoiceFamilyRule; new PreWriteResult)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs (step 5½, RunPreWriteRulesAsync)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs (CheckInvoiceFamilyAsync's admitted decision; KeepRegardingPairWholeAsync, the caller update planner)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard.cs (DeriveResolverFieldsAsync over a record reader)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs (the planner refusal maps an invoice-family refusal through InvoiceFamilyRefused)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs (~:463, the dedicated writer's derive)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/task-045c-notes.md (Q8 (a) section)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/task-045b-notes.md ("Q8 (update side)")</file>
      <file role="test">tests/integration/seam/RecordCreation/ (create, step order)</file>
      <file role="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/ (caller update paths)</file>
      <file role="test">tests/unit/domain/Dataverse/RecordCreation/RecordTableRulesInvoiceFamilyRuleTests.cs (the rule's result)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="branching">`git switch -c task/fm-045d origin/work/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1` (tip c1afee6e02 or later). Then commit this POML first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="order">On the create the derive runs inside step 5½, after step 5's AppendTo (the app-only reads stand on it). It never runs for a system principal (step 5½ already refuses a table with rules).</constraint>
    <constraint source="decision 2026-11-12">A derive failure is a refusal through the existing invoice-family mapping, never "add nothing". `ReadFailedCode` and `ResolverFieldsIncompleteCode` answer as today's undecided or invalid outcome for that code; `RecordNotFoundCode` answers the uniform not-found. No new refusal kind, code, status or text (NFR-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="whole or none">The five fields are written all together (`ToGenericFields` on the generic paths: a blank name or number is written as a clear), overwriting any of them the caller or the planner set, or not at all.</constraint>
    <constraint source="readers">Create: the regarded record app-only (`IGenericEntityService`), the catalog row by table name app-only (`ICommunicationDataverseService.QueryRecordTypeRefAsync`), as the dedicated writers. Caller update paths: both as the caller. App-only update paths: the stored row, the catalog row by table name (a `QueryExpression` on `sprk_recordtype_ref` through `RetrieveMultipleAsync`) and the regarded record, all through the `IGenericEntityService` the path already holds. No path gains a reader of a kind it does not already hold.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no other change">The guard's admit and refuse decisions are unchanged. Do not edit `SecureRootInheritance.cs` or UAC-r2's files (`DirectThreadAccessService.cs`, `DirectMessageParticipantShares.cs`, `SecureChildShareReconciliationJob.cs`, `SecureChildReconciler.cs`). No change under `.claude/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">Commit messages, code comments, test names and notes state the rules only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / §10 / §11">New tests go under KEEP paths only (`tests/integration/**`, `tests/unit/domain/**`). Never run Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests unfiltered; add `&amp;FullyQualifiedName!~Api.Office.`. §11 answers for `PreWriteResult` and any new member. The publish delta is the main session's.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Branch; FULL rigor; re-grep every file:line in the proposal.</step>
    <step order="1">`PreWriteResult` and the delegate change; existing rules and fixtures return it with no assertion change.</step>
    <step order="2">`InvoiceFamilyRule`: on admit, derive and return the five columns; a derive failure through `InvoiceFamilyPreWrite`.</step>
    <step order="3">Step 5½ merges the columns into `item` before step 6.</step>
    <step order="4">Caller update planner: derive as the caller when the update sets or clears a core lookup; the route maps a derive failure through its invoice-family mapping.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests (AC1-AC6), each must-fire run once with the change switched off to show it fails. Build (0 warnings), ArchTests, filtered suites, `dotnet format whitespace --verify-no-changes` on touched files, `notes/task-045d-notes.md`. Commit on `task/fm-045d`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>(Corrected 2026-11-12.) The earlier trigger said the app-only update paths cannot read the catalog row by table name with `IGenericEntityService`. That was wrong: `RetrieveMultipleAsync` runs a `QueryExpression` on `sprk_recordtype_ref` by `sprk_recordlogicalname`. The app-only half is in scope and built (AC7-AC9). STOP only if a derive there would need a reader the path does not hold.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any existing refusal would change its code, status or text, STOP (NFR-07).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AC1 (create must fire): a generic create of each of the six family tables that names one core record writes all five resolver fields of that record (type reference to its catalog row, id lower-case "D", name, url, number), overwriting any of the five the caller sent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC2 (create fail closed): a derive failure refuses the create and writes nothing, through the existing mapping: a catalog read that faults, or no catalog reader, gives `invoice_family_read_failed` (undecided, 500); no catalog row gives `invoice_family_resolver_fields_incomplete` (400); the regarded record missing gives the uniform not-found. A blank name or number is not a refusal (owner, 2026-11-12, option (b)): the row is created with the type, id and URL, and the blank one is left empty.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC3 (create order): the derive runs only after step 5's AppendTo: a caller refused at step 5 causes no derive read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC4 (update must fire, caller paths): a child-record PATCH that moves a family row's core lookup (same core table, and a switch from one core table to another) writes all five fields of the new record in the same PATCH. A derive failure refuses and writes nothing, mapped through `InvoiceFamilyRefused` (the not-found case is the uniform not-found).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC5 (update must not fire): an update that sets or clears no core lookup reads nothing for the derive and writes none of the five fields; a non-family table is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC6 (NFR-07): every existing refusal suite passes with unchanged assertions (`RecordTableRulesInvoiceFamilyRuleTests`, `ChildRecordCreateRefusalContractTests`, `RecordCreationServicePreWriteRuleSeamTests`, `RecordCreationServicePipelineSeamTests`, the invoice-family guard suites).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC7 (update must fire, app-only paths): on the playbook Update Record, the output mapping and the field-mapping push, a write that moves an invoice-family row's core lookup carries the new record's resolver fields in the same write (type bind, id, URL; name and number when the record has them, cleared otherwise). On the push the fields are added after 022c's source gate and the access-column scrub; they are server values, not access columns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC8 (update fail closed, app-only paths): a derive that cannot be done refuses and writes nothing, through the path's existing invoice-family refusal form with the existing codes only: `RefusalException` (code-only message) on the two handlers, the per-child "Not written: …" error on the push. A run as a person answers a missing record as `invoice_family_read_failed`, as the guard does there.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC9 (submission writers unchanged): the dedicated writers' derive still refuses a blank name or number (all five or none), pinned by their existing tests.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <justification>
    <existing>`PreWriteRefusal` (refusal only); `InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard.DeriveResolverFieldsAsync` (dedicated writers); the 045b planner (`KeepRegardingPairWholeAsync`).</existing>
    <extension>Yes: the delegate's return type is widened; the derive and the planner are reused, not forked.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A generic create or a core-lookup move writes a family row whose resolver fields are missing or describe another record; the D-68 key column and every reader of the pair see the wrong record.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">The files in relevant-files.</output>
    <output type="test">Tests under tests/integration/** and tests/unit/domain/**.</output>
    <output type="notes">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/task-045d-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <notes>Added 2026-11-12 from the owner's go on Q8 (a). Create half from 045c's notes, update half from 045b's notes.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
